WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.861
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module,

2
00:00:02.861 --> 00:00:05.225
which takes about fifty
minutes with the lab.

3
00:00:05.225 --> 00:00:09.600
You'll explain why one writer per account
state comes before every other gate.

4
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.789
You'll read the lifecycle
rows of the writer register

5
00:00:12.789 --> 00:00:16.050
and say which writer and
which backstop each row names.

6
00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:20.325
You'll run the register check and the
audit-log scan, and read what they find.

7
00:00:20.325 --> 00:00:23.450
And you'll say what the scan
can't see, and what covers it.

8
00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:26.754
Before you start, you need
the path's prerequisites:

9
00:00:26.754 --> 00:00:32.023
at least the overview of the Federal
Modernization Workbook's Book 03, Microsoft

10
00:00:32.023 --> 00:00:36.900
Automation Modules 1 and 2, and enough
Python to run a script and read JSON.

11
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:39.509
Lab 1 needs Python 3.10 or later,

12
00:00:39.509 --> 00:00:43.788
pytest and a clone of the
repository, and no tenant.

13
00:00:43.788 --> 00:00:48.670
Lab 2 needs a worldwide or GCC
test tenant, never production.
